            {
                "entry_id": "c96a370b-6594-3cb8-96e5-14a2f6f1ce99",
                "word": "days",
                "pos": "noun",
                "lang_code": "en",
                "forms": [],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "b0af5110-974a-3ba9-8bae-bb340ef708d6",
                        "entry_id": "c96a370b-6594-3cb8-96e5-14a2f6f1ce99",
                        "glosses": [
                            "A particular time or period of vague extent."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "plural",
                            "plural-only"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "e2baae6e-b40c-41f5-b567-ddce2e96b8b3",
                                "sense_id": "b0af5110-974a-3ba9-8bae-bb340ef708d6",
                                "text": "Things were more relaxed in Grandpa's days."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "6b14dd5f-b1f3-47f0-bb0a-8f6fc87f73ab",
                                "sense_id": "b0af5110-974a-3ba9-8bae-bb340ef708d6",
                                "text": "His days of being the king are over."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "77dbf8ea-1857-457f-9677-895b318ff313",
                                "sense_id": "b0af5110-974a-3ba9-8bae-bb340ef708d6",
                                "text": "In the old days, […], he gave no evidences of genius whatsoever. He never read me any of his manuscripts, […], and therefore my lack of detection of his promise may in some degree be pardoned. But he had then none of the oddities and mannerisms which I hold to be inseparable from genius, and which struck my attention in after days when I came in contact with the Celebrity."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "30cb0794-1ad4-49ce-97e1-3b8aabeaeed3",
                                "sense_id": "b0af5110-974a-3ba9-8bae-bb340ef708d6",
                                "text": "He read the letter aloud. Sophia listened with the studied air of one for whom, even in these days, a title possessed some surreptitious allurement."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "38aa105a-14c4-4172-94c5-0b7a6965c349",
                                "sense_id": "b0af5110-974a-3ba9-8bae-bb340ef708d6",
                                "text": "With Pi’s removal from Honan, Chang lost his backing in the Kuei-te position and was obliged to relinquish it. In the winter we find him in nearby Po-chou, Anhwei, enjoying the hospitality of the magistrate P’ei Chen, who had been a friend since Chang's Peking days."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "91ac8218-b3df-48c2-bfc8-ca67361116cc",
                                "sense_id": "b0af5110-974a-3ba9-8bae-bb340ef708d6",
                                "text": "The [Washington] Post's proprietor through those turbulent [Watergate] days, Katharine Graham, held a double place in Washington’s hierarchy: at once regal Georgetown hostess and scrappy newshound, ready to hold the establishment to account. That is a very American position."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "72595af2-8527-32c3-b412-07a94e86c686",
                        "entry_id": "c96a370b-6594-3cb8-96e5-14a2f6f1ce99",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Life."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "plural",
                            "plural-only"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "4b0c2002-a478-4abe-84a7-7c2f341508e9",
                                "sense_id": "72595af2-8527-32c3-b412-07a94e86c686",
                                "text": "That's how he ended his days."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
